concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 Children born as a result of artificial conception procedures or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-8 ;
    values:originalText "surrogacy arrangements  (1) This section applies if a child is:  (a) a child of a person under section 60H or 60HB of the Family Law Act 1975; and  (b) either:  (i) a child of the person’s spouse or de facto partner under that section; or  (ii) a biological child of the person’s spouse or de facto partner.  (2) The child is taken for the purposes of this Act:  (a) to be the child of the person and the spouse or de facto partner; and  (b) not to be the child of anyone else.   Preliminary  Part 1  Section 9  Australian Citizenship Act 2007  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "surrogacy arrangements  (1) This section applies if a child is:  (a) a child of a person under section 60H or 60HB of the Family Law Act 1975; and  (b) either:  (i) a child of the person’s spouse or de facto partner under that section; or  (ii) a biological child of the person’s spouse or de facto partner.  (2) The child is taken for the purposes of this Act:  (a) to be the child of the person and the spouse or de facto partner; and  (b) not to be the child of anyone else.   Preliminary  Part 1  Section 9  Australian Citizenship Act 2007  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "aba46aea5b94ce6978f5a7033db6bc3c704a5d86d0038b2f6a5740701ce4a423" ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-8-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-8-ss-2 ;
