concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 Personal identifiers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a personal identifier is any of the following (including any of the following in digital form):  (a) fingerprints or handprints of a person (including those taken using paper and ink or digital livescanning technologies);  (b) a measurement of a person’s height and weight;  (c) a photograph or other image of a person’s face; Note: See section 10A.  (d) an iris scan;  (e) a person’s signature;  (f) any other identifier prescribed by the regulations (except an identifier the obtaining of which would involve the carrying out of an intimate forensic procedure within the meaning of section 23WA of the Crimes Act 1914)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a personal identifier is any of the following (including any of the following in digital form):  (a) fingerprints or handprints of a person (including those taken using paper and ink or digital livescanning technologies);  (b) a measurement of a person’s height and weight;  (c) a photograph or other image of a person’s face; Note: See section 10A.  (d) an iris scan;  (e) a person’s signature;  (f) any other identifier prescribed by the regulations (except an identifier the obtaining of which would involve the carrying out of an intimate forensic procedure within the meaning of section 23WA of the Crimes Act 1914)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "39eea43c1f5713e06cc98f6df93dab816be4152906f255efbcef91442c529f6d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definition of personal identifier" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.19" ;
