doc:sec-26-3-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26(1) Pledge of commitment must be made" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must make a pledge of commitment to become an Australian citizen unless the person:  (a) is aged under 16 at the time the person made the application to become an Australian citizen; or  (b) has a permanent or enduring physical or mental incapacity, at the time the person made the application to become an Australian citizen, that means the person:  (i) is not capable of understanding the nature of the application at that time; or  (ii) is not capable of demonstrating a basic knowledge of the English language at that time; or   Australian citizenship  Part 2 Acquisition of Australian citizenship by application  Division 2  Section 27  Australian Citizenship Act 2007  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (iii) is not capable of demonstrating an adequate knowledge of Australia and of the responsibilities and privileges of Australian citizenship at that time; or  (c) is covered by subsection 21(6), (7) or (8). Note: See section 27 for how the pledge is to be made." ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer .

