doc:sec-36l a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "36L No resumption of citizenship if citizenship ceases under this" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Subdivision  If a person ceases to be an Australian citizen under this Subdivision, Divisions 1 and 2 of this Part do not apply in relation to the person after that cessation. Note: See section 36B for when a person ceases to be an Australian citizen." ;
    cof:pageNumber "81"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-37 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "37 Evidence of Australian citizenship"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-37 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person may make an application to the Minister for evidence of the person’s Australian citizenship. Note: Section 46 sets out application requirements (which may include the payment of a fee). Notice  (2) The Minister may give the person a notice stating that the person is an Australian citizen at a particular time.  (3) The notice must:  (a) be in a form prescribed by the regulations; and  (b) contain any other matter prescribed by the regulations. Identity  (4) The Minister must not give the person such a notice unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity of the person. Note: Division 5 contains the identity provisions. Evidentiary status  (5) A notice is prima facie evidence of the matters in the notice. Cancellation  (6) The Minister may, by writing, cancel a notice given to a person under this section.   Australian citizenship  Part 2 Evidence of Australian citizenship  Division 4  Section 38  Australian Citizenship Act 2007  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person may make an application to the Minister for evidence of the person’s Australian citizenship. Note: Section 46 sets out application requirements (which may include the payment of a fee). Notice  (2) The Minister may give the person a notice stating that the person is an Australian citizen at a particular time.  (3) The notice must:  (a) be in a form prescribed by the regulations; and  (b) contain any other matter prescribed by the regulations. Identity  (4) The Minister must not give the person such a notice unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity of the person. Note: Division 5 contains the identity provisions. Evidentiary status  (5) A notice is prima facie evidence of the matters in the notice. Cancellation  (6) The Minister may, by writing, cancel a notice given to a person under this section.   Australian citizenship  Part 2 Evidence of Australian citizenship  Division 4  Section 38  Australian Citizenship Act 2007  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e4417f99860138d5b0d5f8eb997360f1d40c2e49667234a2951e1b9a1ab51cab" ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-37-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-37-ss-2 ;
