doc:sec-43-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "43(1) Disclosing identifying information" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person’s conduct causes disclosure of identifying information; and  (b) the disclosure is not a permitted disclosure. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both." ;
    cof:pageNumber "87"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-43-ss-1a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "43(1A) Disclosing identifying information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-43-ss-1a ;
    values:originalText "(1A) If:  (a) a disclosure of identifying information is made to a person who is not an entrusted person; and  (b) the disclosure is a permitted disclosure; this section does not apply in relation to any further disclosure of that identifying information by a person who is not an entrusted person. Note 1: A defendant, except for an IGIS official, bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in this subsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code). For IGIS officials, see section 34C of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986. Note 2: Australian Privacy Principle 6 may apply to further disclosures of that identifying information by a person who is not an entrusted person." ;
    skos:definition "(1A) If:  (a) a disclosure of identifying information is made to a person who is not an entrusted person; and  (b) the disclosure is a permitted disclosure; this section does not apply in relation to any further disclosure of that identifying information by a person who is not an entrusted person. Note 1: A defendant, except for an IGIS official, bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in this subsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code). For IGIS officials, see section 34C of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986. Note 2: Australian Privacy Principle 6 may apply to further disclosures of that identifying information by a person who is not an entrusted person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a9efaa209b5a81a2947f87ae3159173ae68dcc4b60cc84553ee284da5e88a78d" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-43 ;
