concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-45d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "45D Dealing with a document after it is condemned as forfeited"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-45d ;
    values:originalText "(1) If, under section 45C, a document is condemned as forfeited to the Commonwealth, it must be dealt with or disposed of (including by being given to another person) in accordance with any direction given by the Minister.  (2) If the Minister considers that the document may be relevant to proceedings in a court or tribunal, then the Minister:  (a) must give a direction for the safe keeping of the document; and  (b) must authorise access to the document for the purposes of those proceedings.  (3) A direction given under this section is not a legislative instrument.   Other matters  Part 3 Other  Division 2  Section 46  Australian Citizenship Act 2007  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If, under section 45C, a document is condemned as forfeited to the Commonwealth, it must be dealt with or disposed of (including by being given to another person) in accordance with any direction given by the Minister.  (2) If the Minister considers that the document may be relevant to proceedings in a court or tribunal, then the Minister:  (a) must give a direction for the safe keeping of the document; and  (b) must authorise access to the document for the purposes of those proceedings.  (3) A direction given under this section is not a legislative instrument.   Other matters  Part 3 Other  Division 2  Section 46  Australian Citizenship Act 2007  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bab5e3425758dffe28d6d5d96b5fdfe03466757ad8dd63047afdcb71965fb90f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-45d-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-45d-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-45d-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.94" .
doc:sec-45d a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45D Dealing with a document after it is condemned as forfeited" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If, under section 45C, a document is condemned as forfeited to the Commonwealth, it must be dealt with or disposed of (including by being given to another person) in accordance with any direction given by the Minister.  (2) If the Minister considers that the document may be relevant to proceedings in a court or tribunal, then the Minister:  (a) must give a direction for the safe keeping of the document; and  (b) must authorise access to the document for the purposes of those proceedings.  (3) A direction given under this section is not a legislative instrument.   Other matters  Part 3 Other  Division 2  Section 46  Australian Citizenship Act 2007  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer .

